<Doc title="The journal service" kicker="Journal · rewrite in progress" section="journal/" siblings={[]}
  description="Ordered, durable logs for many tenants, on Paxos. paros is rewriting it from the ground up, on stronger foundations.">
  <h2 id="what">What it is</h2>
  <p>The goal of paros is a journal service: ordered, durable logs for many tenants on a cell of
  machines. Paxos chooses every record. The data plane has four calls: <code>Write</code>,
  <code>Read</code>, <code>Truncate</code> and <code>SetLeader</code>. The control plane is made of
  paros journals, elections and Paxos flavors too, so there is no external coordination service
  to run.</p>

  <h2 id="now">Being rewritten</h2>
  <p>A first version ran: a daemon on each machine, a CLI, many cells, Biscuit tokens and a
  deterministic simulation with faults on. It taught a lot, and it showed where its foundations
  were too weak. So paros starts again from the bottom:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><b>The consensus core first.</b> <code>paros-consensus</code> holds every Paxos role as a
      sans-IO state machine. Each flavor that it builds gets a TLA+ model before anything is built
      on it.</li>
    <li><b>Then the judges of the core.</b> Model-based trace checking (each run of the code is
      checked against its TLA+ model), deterministic simulation testing (a seed is a run, faults
      on), and coverage-driven simulation that steers the seeds toward the paths not yet run.</li>
    <li><b>Then the journal</b>, designed again on top of the proved core.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The target design is in <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/docs/architecture`}><code>docs/architecture/</code></a>.</p>

  <h2 id="before">The version before the rewrite</h2>
  <p>The whole first version stays at the git tag
  <a href={TAG}><code>v0.2.0-alpha.1</code></a>: <code>parosd</code>, <code>parosctl</code>,
  <code>paros-bench</code>, the Docker Compose demo and the simulation. To run it:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/PierreZ/paros && cd paros
git checkout v0.2.0-alpha.1
docker compose up -d --build
docker compose run --rm init
docker compose run --rm parosctl tenant create acme</code></pre>
  <p>Its <code>DEMO.md</code> is the walk-through. A recap of each removed crate is in
  <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/docs/archive/v0.2.0-alpha.1`}><code>docs/archive/v0.2.0-alpha.1/</code></a>.</p>
</Doc>
